    "note": [
        {
            "structuredValue": [],
            "parallelValue": [],
            "groupedValue": [],
            "value": "This podcast delves into the mystique of crossword puzzles, examining their enduring appeal and considering the ways in which their elegant lattices reflect the societal milieux from which they arise. Included are interview segments with two local solvers: Prof. Stewart Levin of the Stanford Earth Sciences department, and Roz Stubenberg, a Palo Altan who's  been solving puzzles for scores of years. Soundtrack items are enumerated in the \"Works Cited\" attachment.",
